.nh
.TH "BCDOCK" "1" "Jan 2025" "BCDock CLI" "BCDock Manual"

.SH NAME
bcdock-plans-list - List the subscription plans and their active rates


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbcdock plans list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the plans a company can subscribe to, cheapest active rate first, with each
plan's environment cap. The same catalogue as the pricing page.

.PP
Auth: any API key scope (reference data, the same for every company).

.PP
Exit codes:
  0   ok
  3   auth failure (missing or invalid token)
  4   rate-limited


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env: BCDOCK_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colored output

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, csv

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Request timeout

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	API token (env: BCDOCK_TOKEN)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  bcdock plans list
  bcdock plans list -o json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBbcdock-plans(1)\fP
